<title>MEXICO: Mexico silver output rises, other metals detailed.</title>
<headline>Mexico silver output rises, other metals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest silver producer, saw output rise in November to 216,314 kg from the 200,666 kg produced in November 1995, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said Thursday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of metals and minerals production in the January-November period follows:  </p>
<p>    Product     Nov 96     Nov 95     Jan-Nov   Pct Chge Vs 95</p>
<p>    Gold	   2,505	1,904	21,822	  20.7</p>
<p>    Silver     216,314    200,666   2,298,504	   0.3</p>
<p>    Lead	  14,726     13,358     150,045	 -10.1</p>
<p>    Copper	26,121     33,204     297,493	  -4.9</p>
<p>    Zinc	  30,226     29,315     316,270	  -2.7</p>
<p>    Coal	 768,321    820,874   7,830,610	  23.0</p>
<p>    Iron	 407,316    454,010   5,549,344	  11.2</p>
<p>    Sulphur     70,571     65,000     843,994	   6.1</p>
<p>    Dolomite    77,500    100,902     846,482	   N/A</p>
<p>    Gypsum     325,155    284,409   3,399,656	   6.0</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 61,806     55,865     622,873	   N/A</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kilos, others in tonnes. Coal output in mineral volume. Figures revised from January-October figures given by INEGI.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530.</p>
</text>
